        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "The Jami Masjid of Champaner, located within the Champaner-Pavagadh Archaeological Park (a UNESCO World Heritage Site in Gujarat), is one of the finest surviving examples of pre-Mughal Indo-Islamic architecture in India. Built primarily during the late 15th century under the patronage of Sultan Mahmud Begada of the Gujarat Sultanate, it served as the principal congregational mosque of the once-thriving capital city of Champaner.",
